on decisions and does not control physical hardware.\",\n  \"No push or SMS delivery is added beyond contract-defined API behavior; reporting and settings are limited to contract-defined operations without scheduled email dispatch or a custom report builder.\",\n  \"Office release configuration is administrator-managed in PostgreSQL through contract configuration operations; the contract example initial timezone and release time are `Asia/Karachi` and `08:00`, and the initial scheduling window is 30 days.\",\n  \"Parking dates and times use the configured office-local timezone, initially `Asia/Karachi`, and use the persisted office timezone after an administrator changes it.\",\n  \"Demo seeding is idempotent: it inserts only when contract-defined identifiers are absent and does not overwrite or delete existing records.\",\n  \"Tests use isolated databases and provision their own fixtures rather than relying on demo seed rows, except for seed-specific acceptance checks.\",\n  \"The drafts contain different sample-row count interpretations; these are retained as separate requirements rather than resolved by an assumption.\"\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [],\n \"outOfScope\": [\n  \"Physical camera/LPR acquisition and physical indicator-light actuation; the API accepts detection requests and returns verification decisions only.\",\n  \"Push and SMS notification delivery beyond behavior expressly defined by the API contract.\",\n  \"Automated scheduled weekly or Monday report-email delivery and custom report-builder functionality; contract-defined reporting operations remain in scope.\",\n  \"External corporate-directory synchronization; employee profile, assignment, and directory-source records are maintained in PostgreSQL.\",\n  \"Email/password sign-in and reset-link flows, superseded by the locked OpenAPI contract's Google identity token and OAuth2 security.\"\n ],\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A valid Google identity token identifies an allowed Folio3 Google Workspace employee, and the session-creation operation has no bearer-token requirement.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the returned session contains the contract-required access token, token type, expiry, employee identity, corporate email, and administrator flag.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends the token as `googleIdentityToken` to `POST /auth/sessions`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A session request is malformed or has a missing token, or the identity token is invalid or unauthorized.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 400 for malformed or missing input, or 401 for an invalid or unauthorized identity, and the response body conforms to the contract `ApiError` schema for the applicable error.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends the request to `POST /auth/sessions`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An employee has a valid authenticated session and profile and vehicle records.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned profile conforms to `EmployeeProfile`, identifies the authenticated employee, and includes the contract-defined employee fields, assigned parking status, assigned floor, and vehicles; an unauthenticated request has response status 401 and an authenticated identity without permission has response status 403.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee requests `GET /me/profile`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An employee has a valid authenticated session and registered vehicles.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned `vehicles` list conforms to `VehicleList` and contains only that employee's vehicles; a request without authentication has response status 401.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee requests `GET /me/vehicles`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An employee has a valid authenticated session and submits a vehicle-registration request with a plate and optional vehicle details.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.5\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the returned vehicle conforms to `Vehicle`, contains the submitted fields, and has status `Active`; invalid input has response status 400, missing authentication has response status 401, and a conflicting registration has response status 409, with each error response conforming to the contract `ApiError` schema.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee sends the request to `POST /me/vehicles`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 31,\n     \"lineStart\": 28,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"app.MapGet(\\\"/\\\", () => \\\"API is up\\\").ExcludeFromDescription();\\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\\napp.MapOpenApi();\\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\\\"/openapi/v1.json\\\", \\\"API\\\"));\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 15,\n     \"lineStart\": 8,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"security:\\n  - oauth2:\\n      - parking:access\\npaths:\\n  /auth/sessions:\\n    post:\\n      operationId: createSession\\n      summary: Create a session from a Folio3 Google Workspace identity\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking API shall implement `POST /auth/sessions`, `GET /me/profile`, and `GET` and `POST /me/vehicles` with the request schemas, response schemas, security, and status behavior declared in the locked OpenAPI contract.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-5\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An authenticated employee requests the office configuration and the office has its contract-example initial configuration.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response body conforms to `ParkingConfig`, with `officeTimezone` `Asia/Karachi`, `releaseTime` `08:00`, `schedulingWindowDays` 30, working days, and the holiday setting; a request without authentication has response status 401.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee requests `GET /parking/config`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An employee has a valid authenticated session and parking data for the current office-local date.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response body conforms to `ParkingHome` and contains the office-local date and timezone, employee assignment and parking status, space status, release time, availability count, and contract-required vehicle and working-day fields; a request without authentication has response status 401.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee requests `GET /parking/today`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 31,\n     \"lineStart\": 28,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"app.MapGet(\\\"/\\\", () => \\\"API is up\\\").ExcludeFromDescription();\\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\\napp.MapOpenApi();\\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\\\"/openapi/v1.json\\\", \\\"API\\\"));\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking API shall implement `GET /parking/config` and `GET /parking/today` using the configured office-local date and time and contract-defined response schemas; initial office configuration uses `Asia/Karachi`, release time `08:00`, and a 30-day scheduling window.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"ASM-7\",\n    \"ASM-8\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An a