00 and the returned report conforms to `UtilizationReport` and contains the requested week dates, generation time, office timezone, released-space and temporary-claim counts, utilization percentage, daily statistics, and unused dedicated and temporary parking lists; an invalid date has response status 400, a request without authentication has response status 401, and a non-administrator receives response status 403.\",\n     \"when\": \"The administrator requests `GET /admin/utilization` with an optional `weekStart`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A dedicated holder did not release a space and has no registered-vehicle entry record for a date, and a temporary claimant has no registered-vehicle entry record for a date.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned report lists contain the corresponding `Unused Dedicated Parking` and `Unused Temporary Parking` events with employee, vehicle plate, and office-local date.\",\n     \"when\": \"An administrator requests the corresponding week through `GET /admin/utilization`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An authenticated standard employee requests a utilization report.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 403 and the response error code is `forbidden`.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee requests `GET /admin/utilization`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 31,\n     \"lineStart\": 28,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"app.MapGet(\\\"/\\\", () => \\\"API is up\\\").ExcludeFromDescription();\\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\\napp.MapOpenApi();\\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\\\"/openapi/v1.json\\\", \\\"API\\\"));\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking API shall implement `GET /admin/utilization` to return contract-defined office-local weekly statistics and unused dedicated and temporary parking records derived from retained parking and entrance data, with administrator authorization.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"ASM-6\",\n    \"ASM-8\",\n    \"ASM-3\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An authenticated parking administrator has office settings stored in the application database.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the returned `OfficeSettings` contains office timezone, release time, scheduling-window days, report recipients, report schedule, and next delivery; a request without authentication has response status 401 and a non-administrator receives response status 403.\",\n     \"when\": \"The administrator requests `GET /admin/settings`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An authenticated parking administrator submits valid office timezone, release time, and report-recipient values.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Both response statuses are 200 and the returned settings preserve the submitted timezone, release time, and recipient values and include the contract-defined schedule fields; invalid values have response status 400, a request without authentication has response status 401, and a non-administrator receives response status 403.\",\n     \"when\": \"The administrator sends the values to `PUT /admin/settings` and then reads `GET /admin/settings`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An authenticated standard employee submits or reads office settings.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 403 and the response error code is `forbidden`.\",\n     \"when\": \"The employee calls `PUT` or `GET /admin/settings`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 31,\n     \"lin